From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Recreate the toplevel role when adding server
 side decorations.

The server side decoration support creates a zxdg_toplevel_decoration_v1
when an existing toplevel gains a caption. xdg-decoration does not allow
that once the toplevel has a buffer attached or committed: the
compositor raises unconfigured_buffer ("xdg_toplevel_decoration must not
have a buffer at creation") and drops the connection, which takes the
whole process down.

Battlefield 4 does this when it is alt-tabbed and when graphics settings
are applied, and crashed both times.

Give the window a new toplevel role instead. wayland_surface_clear_role()
detaches the buffer, so the decoration is created before the new
toplevel's first commit, like for a window that is mapped with a
caption. Removing decorations from a mapped toplevel is allowed and
stays as it was.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -1664,13 +1664,20 @@
             surface->zxdg_toplevel_decoration_v1 = NULL;
             surface->pending.decor = surface->current.decor = 0;
         }
-        else if (server_decor && !surface->zxdg_toplevel_decoration_v1)
-            wayland_surface_init_decoration(surface);
 
-        wl_surface_commit(surface->wl_surface);
-        wl_display_flush(process_wayland.wl_display);
+        if (!server_decor || surface->zxdg_toplevel_decoration_v1)
+        {
+            wl_surface_commit(surface->wl_surface);
+            wl_display_flush(process_wayland.wl_display);
+            return;
+        }
 
-        return;
+        /* A decoration can only be created for a toplevel that has no buffer
+         * attached or committed yet, otherwise the compositor raises
+         * unconfigured_buffer and drops our connection. The window gained a
+         * caption after it was mapped (e.g. when leaving fullscreen), so give
+         * it a new toplevel role that is decorated from the start. */
+        TRACE("hwnd=%p recreating the toplevel role for server side decorations\n", surface->hwnd);
     }
 
     wayland_surface_clear_role(surface);
